FLOP publishes a hosted MCP server for the network itself: 34 read-only tools — chain stats, settlements, model pricing.

LUMI now reads that instead of a hard-coded price. An agent should price compute from the tape, not from vibes.

{link}

Most agent stacks assume an inference price. FLOP's settlements carry the price per GFLOP that was actually paid.

We archive the median/min/max daily and size the channel budget from it. First number beats the first opinion.

{link}

Agent grants on FLOP unlock by spending: 3 FLOP of compute, 1 FLOP liquid, capped at three quarters of principal.

So an agent that sits idle stays locked. Budget the spend path before the grant lands, not after.

{link}
